	(text "PG->EN DIVIDER ARITHMETIC (F34) -- check before any BOM cost-pass normalises these values.\nPGOOD on U3 is OPEN-DRAIN (T1-64). Three constraints on two resistors:\n  1. PG released (+3V3_D up): EN_3V3_PLL = 3V3 * R3/(R2+R3) must exceed the LDO's V_IH.\n  2. PG asserted low (fault): EN must sit below V_IL.\n  3. +3V3_D absent / PG high-Z: R3 must dominate so EN defaults LOW -- fail-safe off.\nValues above are PLACEHOLDERS. [VERIFY] the chosen LDO's EN threshold table, then solve.\nDo not substitute standard values without re-checking all three inequalities."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 199.39000000000001 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "f4b771e1-8b5b-5b70-b53f-3f0aaabea8d2")
	)
	(text "SCOPE: this pass places active devices, dispositions every pin, and defines the\nsequencing and monitor nets. Inductors, bulk/bypass caps and feedback dividers are the\nnext pass -- FB/SW/CBOOT/SET/ILIM pins carry named nets, not no-connects, so nothing\nis left undispositioned in the meantime (F28)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 250.19 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "a768b167-9757-59f2-a96b-686ddce98501")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
